   202	- SENTENCE LAW (the most important paper standard — a paper nobody can follow is a
   203	  failed paper regardless of its numbers). Every sentence must survive four tests,
   204	  each shown with a real failure from rehearsal and its fix:
   205	  1. SIMPLE + EXACT: plain words making a precise claim. If you cannot say exactly
   206	     what a sentence claims, it is broken no matter how simple it sounds.
   207	     BAD:  "Putting more text in a prompt changes more than the amount a model must
   208	           read." (changes more WHAT? the comparison never lands)
   209	     GOOD: "Increasing document length can also change the answer's relative position and
